From: SM-X910 postmarketOS port <gts9uwifi@example.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/mdss: optionally power-cycle MDSS before child probe

Some boot chains leave the display power domain in a state which is neither
usable by the upstream driver nor repaired by the MDSS block reset.  A full
system suspend fixes the display because genpd power-collapses MDSS before the
DSI host and PHY are brought up again.

Allow affected boards to request the same clean boundary before DPU/DSI child
devices are populated.  Keeping this opt-in avoids changing probe behaviour on
other Qualcomm platforms.

Signed-off-by: SM-X910 postmarketOS port <gts9uwifi@example.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_mdss.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_mdss.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_mdss.c
index 531669198ef2..e2f2462e6097 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_mdss.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_mdss.c
@@ -480,6 +480,28 @@ static int mdss_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, mdss);
 
+	if (device_property_read_bool(dev, "qcom,initial-power-cycle")) {
+		/*
+		 * The runtime-PM status starts suspended.  Resume once so the
+		 * PM core owns the complete parent/genpd state, then suspend
+		 * synchronously to guarantee a real GDSC power collapse before
+		 * any DPU, DSI or PHY child probes.  Their first runtime get will
+		 * bring the hierarchy back from a known-off state.
+		 */
+		ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(dev);
+		if (ret < 0) {
+			msm_mdss_destroy(mdss);
+			return ret;
+		}
+
+		ret = pm_runtime_put_sync_suspend(dev);
+		if (ret < 0) {
+			msm_mdss_destroy(mdss);
+			return ret;
+		}
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * MDP5/DPU based devices don't have a flat hierarchy. There is a top
 	 * level parent: MDSS, and children: MDP5/DPU, DSI, HDMI, eDP etc.
-- 
2.50.1
